[40.67785, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[6d\b\u001b[38;5;243m◆ reading: Read the pantry inventory and write shopping-plan.md. Qua… · \"Read the pantry inventory and\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;243mwrite shopping-plan.md. Quantities are packages; below 3 packages is low. Buying stays manual. I want\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;243mweekly reviews and a project rule requiring permission before inventory edits. First draft the plan and\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;243midentify ambiguities; do not schedule anything yet.\"\u001b[m\u001b[48X\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mdone\u001b[m\u001b[92X\u001b[11;105H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mWritten to \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1596/project/shopping-plan.md\u0007/tmp/caf-extended-1596/project/shopping-plan.md\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007. It carries the threshold\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mrule (low = \u001b[48;5;234mquantity < 3\u001b[49m packages), the weekly-review and manual-buying rules, the\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mpermission-before-edit rule for \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1596/project/pantry.csv\u0007pantry.csv\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007, the current low list from \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1596/project/pantry.csv\u0007pantry.csv\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007 (beans\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m0, rice 2; tea 5 is fine), and a section of open ambiguities.\u001b[m\u001b[16;105H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mThe ambiguities to settle before this is final:\u001b[m\u001b[18;105H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m1.\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[1mREADME contradicts the request.\u001b[22m \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1596/project/README.md\u0007README.md\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007 describes building a Python CLI that\u001b[m\u001b[22X\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   reports items below a threshold — not a markdown plan. Is the deliverable this file,\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   the CLI, or both?\u001b[m\u001b[32X\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m2.\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[1mBoundary of \"below 3\".\u001b[22m Strict \u001b[48;5;234m< 3\u001b[49m (my assumption, so 3 is not low) or \u001b[48;5;234m<= 3\u001b[49m? The\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   current table is unaffected either way, but it changes future reviews.\u001b[m\u001b[28X\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m3.\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[1mNo target/par level.\u001b[22m How far to restock a low item (beans to 3? to 5?) — not\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   derivable from the file.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m4.\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[1mWeekly review mechanics.\u001b[22m Which day/time, who runs it, and what forces an off-cycle\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   review (an item hitting 0?).\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m5.\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[1mWhere the permission rule lives\u001b[22m (\u001b[48;5;234mRULES.md\u001b[49m / \u001b[48;5;234mCONTRIBUTING\u001b[49m / README), who grants\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   permission, and whether it also covers \u001b[48;5;234mshopping-plan.md\u001b[49m or only \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1596/project/pantry.csv\u0007pantry.csv\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m6.\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[1mStale data.\u001b[22m \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1596/project/pantry.csv\u0007pantry.csv\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007 has no last-updated date, so \"weekly\" is unanchored.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m7.\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[1mData completeness.\u001b[22m No units, brands, budget or lead times, so quantities stop at\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   package counts.\u001b[m\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;252mNothing is scheduled, as you asked — the weekly review and the permission rule are\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mrecorded as rules in the plan, not as standing items. When you want them to persist\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mbeyond this chat, say so and I'll propose them.\u001b[m\u001b[38;65H\u001b[38;5;243m───── \u001b[m   \u001b[38;5;252m$0.01\u001b[38;5;243m · \u001b[38;5;252m⟲ 81% cached\u001b[38;5;243m   \u001b[38;5;252m17.2k/1M · 2%\u001b[m   \u001b[38;5;243mchecking · \u001b[m\n\u001b[4G\u001b[?25h"]
