and what forces an off-cycle review (an\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103mitem hitting 0?).\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103m5. **Where the permission rule lives** (`RULES.md` / `CONTRIBUTING` / README), who grants permission,\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103mand whether it also covers `shopping-plan.md` or only `pantry.csv`.\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103m6. **Stale data.** `pantry.csv` has no last-updated date, so \"weekly\" is unanchored.\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103m7. **Data completeness.** No units, brands, budget or lead times, so quantities stop at package\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103mcounts.\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103mNothing is scheduled, as you asked — the weekly review and the permission rule are recorded as rules\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103min the plan, not as standing items. When you want them to persist beyond this chat, say so and I'll\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103mpropose them.\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;243m╰─▶ read\u001b[m\u001b[92X\u001b[36;105H\u001b[38;5;110m○\u001b[m\u001b[39;4H\u001b[?25h"]
